Marvel Ultimate Alliance Gold Edition's scene profile for the scene upscaler of 0161 to 0166. The Gold Edition links a
later Direct3D, which also draws full-surface quads over the scene surface's EDRAM at 4x MSAA with half the pitch (the
same width in samples), on its color (base 0) and depth (base 1128), between the scene's draws and resolves. Draws at
another sample count end the scene's pass, so the mua1-gold profile keeps 0166's rule and adds scene_memory_4x_draws:
until the frame's scene is done, those draws are part of its pass, drawn at the scene's scale without jitter, and the
planes they write over count as cleared for the depth taken once between clears (ScenePlanes::Clear, which a
resolve's clears go through too). Any other draw between the scene's resolves still ends its pass, and a second pass
in a frame still turns the upscaler off. mua1 leaves it off, so Marvel Ultimate Alliance is unchanged.

